          "paragraphs": [
            "The Mill Shirt was what the weavers wore to work, and it's cut the same way it was in 1948: long in the body, roomy in the arm, with a two-button cuff and a chest pocket sized for a pencil and a notebook. 12 oz wool, fulled after weaving so it sheds a light rain. Buttons are horn.",
            "Wool this heavy needs a shirt under it, and it's warm enough that you'll take it off indoors. It'll last a couple of decades if you keep the moths off it and don't put it in a dryer."
          ],
          "tradeoff": "Too warm to wear indoors.",
